lity":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.07919451566675703,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":99.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.014152580752232247,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":32.3,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.24555,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Natural Resource Partners L.P., together with its subsidiaries, owns, manages, and leases a portfolio of mineral properties in the United States. It operates in two segments, Mineral Rights and Soda Ash. It owns interests in coal, soda ash, trona, and other natural resources. The company's coal reserves are primarily located in the Appalachia Basin, the Illinois Basin, and the Northern Powder River Basin in the United States; industrial minerals and aggregates properties located in the United States; and oil and gas properties located in Louisiana. It leases a portion of its reserves in exchange for royalty payments; and owns and leases transportation and processing infrastructure related to coal properties. Natural Resource Partners L.P. was incorporated in 2002 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Corbin J. Robertson Jr. | Chairman & CEO of GP Natural Resource Partners LLC | Age 78 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","financial_summary":["Natural Resource Partners LP Li is a small-cap energy business with a $1.6B market cap.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and -5% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","The business throws off $166M in free cash flow, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.22\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 18\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 7.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 25% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Carries a 49% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.4871681415929203},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","23 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Understanding the Setup: (NRP) and Scalable Risk","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/90/Understanding_the_Setup:_NRP_and_Scalable_Ris